{"results":[{"id":"6a3ae5bf02925732fd075068","name":"Observed phishing URLs delivering RMM payload","description":"ScreenConnect is used in phishing URLs to deliver RMM payload. DocuSign has been observed to be the common theme in these phishing emails.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-06-23T19:59:58.474000","created":"2026-06-23T19:59:58.474000","revision":1,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4426909055,"indicator":"https:\/\/vy.ijnggpi.com\/ftx\/","type":"URL","created":"2026-06-23T20:00:00","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4426909057,"indicator":"https:\/\/web-g63lkz.screenconnect.com\/Bin\/ScreenConnect.ClientSetup.msi","type":"URL","created":"2026-06-23T20:00:00","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4426909058,"indicator":"a30a9779079dc897a15fed27f27f614fab77a20e953368808ba99ac6c6a3375b","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-23T20:00:00","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["phishing","screenconnect","rmm","docusign"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["ScreenConnect"],"attack_ids":["T1566","T1133","T1036"],"references":["https:\/\/x.com\/patialavii\/status\/2068919332126835122"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a3ac3d87dd519f2fec1d2ea","name":"A Multi-Stage Steganographic Loader Campaign Deploying Diverse Payloads Globally","description":"A sophisticated phishing campaign was identified distributing multiple malware families through a multi-stage loader utilizing steganography and fileless techniques. The infection chain begins with archive attachments containing files disguised as financial documents, primarily targeting Indian organizations using names related to GST, NEFT, RTGS, and IMPS transactions. The loader employs in-memory execution to avoid disk-based artifacts and uses embedded .NET Bitmap objects to conceal payloads. Various malware families have been deployed including Remcos RAT, Agent Tesla, MassLogger, Phantom Stealer, Dark Cloud, Red Line Stealer, Snake keyloggers, Formbook, and xworm. The final payloads establish persistence through registry Run keys, perform process hollowing, steal browser credentials, record audio and webcam, and exfiltrate data to command-and-control infrastructure. The campaign exhibits characteristics of a loader-as-a-service operation serving multiple threat actors globally.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-06-23T19:27:18.212000","created":"2026-06-23T17:35:20.095000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4400084210,"indicator":"372f19a45d0eb4c8c52117c6ae2bb8040a91bc72be8670623f957a18c2166985","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-23T17:35:20","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427178050,"indicator":"897abf678edad72998554ec18675092f","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-23T17:35:20","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427178051,"indicator":"afe085b7324d72673eef749ff5f21a49","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-23T17:35:20","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427178052,"indicator":"c2e25aba8e2ad4cafdd6c633b8ca0906","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-23T17:35:20","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427178053,"indicator":"be36ef651eed6808760153200a3a2a2b7060cce5","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-06-23T17:35:20","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427558707,"indicator":"4924369c0bdaf73b21eb992eb9db4dea","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-23T17:35:20","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427558708,"indicator":"f3626a38fcf488c9eed54beb8c7c116f","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-23T17:35:20","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["fileless","loader-as-a-service","steganography","phantom stealer","formbook","masslogger","infostealer","dark cloud","remcos rat","phishing campaign","red line stealer","xworm","snake","process hollowing","agent tesla","credential theft"],"targeted_countries":["British Indian Ocean Territory","India"],"malware_families":["Remcos RAT","Agent Tesla - S0331","MassLogger","Phantom Stealer","Dark Cloud","Red Line Stealer","EKANS - S0605","SNAKEHOSE","Formbook","xworm"],"attack_ids":["T1113","T1218.011","T1056.001","T1123","T1497.001","T1566.001","T1005","T1140","T1112","T1555.003","T1125","T1083","T1041","T1059.001","T1547.001","T1055.012","T1027","T1564.001"],"references":["https:\/\/labs.k7computing.com\/index.php\/a-multi-stage-steganographic-loader-campaign-deploying-diverse-payloads-globally"],"industries":["Finance"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a3add255a93c4e851962479","name":"The #APT36 cluster can't stop, won't stop","description":"They just added #CVE-2026-21509 and #CVE-2026-21513 (borrowed from APT28) onto their delivery chain, pushing updated FIREPOWER via weaponized RTF and LNKs against \ud83c\uddee\ud83c\uddf3 targets. Separately, fresh SheetCreep + a shiny new CrystalShell-Slack variant co-dropped on a Kashmir target, because one implant is never enough. The vibeware factory is running three shifts: Crystal, .NET and PowerShell.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-06-23T19:23:16.604000","created":"2026-06-23T19:23:16.604000","revision":1,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"APT36","indicators":[{"id":4426909127,"indicator":"6df13b336f3daccc29a5f24bd5824f4ae9b4d7c45ee9c9adcd7a36679ee009c5","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-23T19:23:18","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4426909128,"indicator":"558dd73f708d4ea7b33fec295ac201ee5c76ba293856d8835225538c11ff208e","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-23T19:23:18","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4426909129,"indicator":"9a93231038c7807c7c1376de1546cae94b6778106bb2ef115631da0991adbb91","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-23T19:23:18","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4426909130,"indicator":"12335f9a1b7d3b84d2844b42f6f2ae03b70c2cc3d68e6c2dd468ee1ec6b2f3c1","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-23T19:23:18","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4426909131,"indicator":"3d74a0fb447590ba7c054e6e7c6d182d145651f588aa4de8bf0972461d9652f2","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-23T19:23:18","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["apt36","turkey","firepower","lnk","rtf","crystalshell"],"targeted_countries":["T\u00fcrkiye"],"malware_families":["SHEETCREEP","CrystalShell"],"attack_ids":[],"references":["https:\/\/x.com\/GenThreatLabs\/status\/2068972067307811234"],"industries":["Government"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a3ab4c93adb7c2764a5fa23","name":"Customer CRM Data Accessed in Supply Chain Incident","description":"LastPass experienced a security incident through Klue, a third-party market intelligence platform integrated with its Salesforce and Gong systems. On June 12, 2026, LastPass was notified that an unauthorized actor exploited stolen OAuth tokens held by Klue to access customer relationship management data within LastPass's Salesforce environment. The exposed information includes customer names, email addresses, phone numbers, physical addresses, support case data, and sales records. Multiple Klue customers were affected by this supply chain attack. LastPass confirmed no Gong data was accessed, and customer vaults, master passwords, and encrypted vault data remain unaffected. The company has terminated Klue access, rotated compromised API tokens, and is cooperating with law enforcement while warning customers about potential phishing attempts using the exposed contact information.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-06-23T19:14:35.694000","created":"2026-06-23T16:31:05.410000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4417670541,"indicator":"138.226.246.94","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-06-23T16:31:06","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-07-23T16:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4417670543,"indicator":"94.154.32.160","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-06-23T16:31:06","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-07-23T16:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4418528171,"indicator":"baccarat.com.au","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-23T16:31:06","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["salesforce","phishing risk","supply chain attack","lastpass","third-party vendor compromise","oauth tokens","crm data breach","klue"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1213.002","T1114","T1566.002","T1566.001","T1530","T1589.002","T1589.003","T1552.001","T1528","T1098.001","T1199","T1098","T1078","T1486","T1567.002","T1598","T1213","T1071.001","T1550.001","T1078.004"],"references":["https:\/\/cyberpress.org\/lastpass-confirms-customer-crm\/"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a3ac05e2137f66d3a690558","name":"From PostCSS Masquerading to Windows RAT","description":"A sophisticated supply chain attack leverages typosquatting of the legitimate postcss-selector-parser npm package, which receives over 150 million weekly downloads. Three malicious packages published by user 'abdrizak' masquerade as PostCSS utilities while delivering a multi-stage Windows RAT. The infection chain begins with encoded JavaScript that drops PowerShell scripts, which then download a bundled Python runtime containing Nuitka-compiled modules. The final payload implements comprehensive RAT capabilities including HTTP C2 communication with RC4 encryption, registry persistence, VM detection, remote shell execution, file transfer, and Chrome credential theft using DPAPI and app-bound decryption. The attack demonstrates how build tooling dependencies can serve as delivery mechanisms for sophisticated Windows malware targeting developer environments.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-06-23T19:10:09.570000","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:30.433000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4427550671,"indicator":"208166120775a11cb6680139ea0f3372","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550672,"indicator":"4c1bdb2b045debf5b25e5be540ef99f0","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550673,"indicator":"c2875e2f45e5f1dfa04463de53b3fa5a","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550674,"indicator":"c5207f87b9103634b4db6f120eb6172a","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550675,"indicator":"f189c338a5f2bc3cce06cee37c0b7522","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550676,"indicator":"2890d90edfc08fb4cfafe0d5fa2a9fb6800dedf5","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550677,"indicator":"71c6cd37ddc0e5899174c72eefee8b224fd1f4bb","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550678,"indicator":"7b1919c35da92cf5fd2583783dc9364fd11b69d2","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550679,"indicator":"8e162d4fc8c5c74e16bfb4346f893cc7a71c2476","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550680,"indicator":"965e3d19c89f12ef730120b84d9ee38755841447","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550681,"indicator":"164e322d6fbc62e254d73583acd7f39444c884d3f5e6a5d27db143fc25bc88b3","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550682,"indicator":"17832aa629524ef6e8d8d6e9b6b902a8d324b559e3c36dbd0e221ab1690be871","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550683,"indicator":"282b9bc318ad1234cbd1b86424b784299b8be31545802a7c6b751166b814b990","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550684,"indicator":"50ffce607867d8fa8eaf6ef5cd25a3c0e7e4415e881b9e55c04a67bcddb74fdf","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550685,"indicator":"c8075bbff748096e1c6a1ea0aa67bb6762fdd7551427a12425b35b94c1f1ecf2","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550686,"indicator":"f6669bd504ce6b0e303be7ee47f2ebbc062989c88c41f0a3f436044a24869798","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550688,"indicator":"http:\/\/nvidiadriver.net\/verv1432\/winpatch-xd7d.win","type":"URL","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550689,"indicator":"nvidiadriver.net","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427550690,"indicator":"winpatch-xd7d.win","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-23T17:20:31","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["rat","multistage","supply chain","python","typosquatting","postcss","nuitka","credential theft","npm"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1204.002","T1573.001","T1497.001","T1082","T1106","T1005","T1140","T1555","T1112","T1555.003","T1134.002","T1041","T1059.001","T1547.001","T1027","T1195.002","T1027.002","T1071.001","T1059.005","T1105"],"references":["https:\/\/research.jfrog.com\/post\/from-postcss-typosquat-to-windows-rat"],"industries":["Technology"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a3a780ee89db8a716522418","name":"Artifact scanner detects npm package 'node-fetch-utils' using external dependency resolution with remote tarball dependency from GitHub","description":"A malicious npm package named 'node-fetch-utils' was discovered masquerading as a legitimate fetch helper utility. The package declares a remote tarball dependency from GitHub that executes upon installation. It runs an obfuscated postinstall script targeting Windows systems, which downloads a bundled Python runtime and drops it as Microsoft\\EdgeBroker\\pythonw.exe for persistence. The dropper then uses this disguised runtime to execute a fileless Python implant decrypted in memory and launched hidden via wscript. The dropper scripts self-delete while the disguised runtime remains active on the compromised system, establishing command and control communications.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-06-23T19:07:34.088000","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:58.863000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4426909094,"indicator":"http:\/\/node22.lunes.host:3258","type":"URL","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4426909095,"indicator":"4ce45e016a304d813e67b29a08265b2101c2e15a09ace5de6539cad02567affe","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427169373,"indicator":"7bd07e4d557852446a284d038fa0ed0e","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427169374,"indicator":"191f6b9a3bc7f0f01c6aaae6485b7bf85e6c12f4","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["python implant","obfuscated script","node-fetch-utils","javascript dropper","dependency confusion","supply chain attack","node-fetch-core","npm","persistence","fileless malware"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["node-fetch-utils","node-fetch-core"],"attack_ids":["T1059.007","T1036.005","T1574.001","T1140","T1055","T1547.001","T1027","T1195.002","T1564.003","T1070.004","T1071.001","T1059.005","T1105"],"references":["https:\/\/x.com\/nextronresearch\/status\/2068958596646265033"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a3a7809c43cfba36348ed9d","name":"PHISH ALERT: From a Simple Phishing Email to a Full Attack Arsenal: The Evolution of \"ClickFix\"","description":"A sophisticated phishing campaign leverages evolved ClickFix techniques to bypass modern endpoint security through victim-assisted execution. Targets receive emails with urgent OneDrive document lures containing malicious ZIP attachments. The attack uses LNK shortcuts that redirect victims to landing pages, silently injecting PowerShell commands into their clipboard. Through social engineering, victims are tricked into manually executing commands via Win+R, circumventing traditional security filters. The campaign employs DNS TXT records for payload staging, avoiding HTTP detection. The threat infrastructure hosts multiple malicious components including obfuscated scripts, fake MSI installers masquerading as legitimate software like ConnectWise, and ISO images with spyware for persistent access. This represents a shift toward long-game tactics focused on establishing full post-compromise environmental control.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-06-23T19:06:19.140000","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:53.706000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":3454363957,"indicator":"italy-news.info","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:54","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4201737801,"indicator":"lootrioya.info","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:54","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4426910336,"indicator":"document-auth.icu","type":"domain","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:54","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4426910340,"indicator":"7b7981c99d59595fe15377df84695bb72ce0b85560a3935f930657b2d162e5ef","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:54","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4426910341,"indicator":"adcd15f3d6b87f84d106ea426fa824fd20c9d64f6d199ce92580884290785f30","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:54","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4426910342,"indicator":"d7d2f0ee187549f3f4a114d716be12521fbf62d6d26e2ac23d2a32d521d08fd8","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:54","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427100060,"indicator":"79e205576bdad2cce593ae850b0c9e31","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:54","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427100061,"indicator":"e5989c374fa9cb1bc53b202032257a3c","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:54","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427100062,"indicator":"5442dea013b109ac4d0cdc52248b758a6cb9684c","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:54","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427100063,"indicator":"e46d05b8aa8f1b1a5e81da2ebe2bf8e94cbe85fe","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:54","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427169359,"indicator":"7596699747d2b284df77d2c83714aa00","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:54","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4427169360,"indicator":"5cf01e24f6bafa64815d1bd2f3323ea091d504cc","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-06-23T12:11:54","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["credential harvesting","clickfix","phishing campaign","dns txt staging","rmm tools","powershell","spyware","social engineering"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1053.005","T1560.001","T1132.001","T1056.001","T1071.004","T1204.002","T1566.002","T1566.001","T1553.002","T1082","T1218.007","T1140","T1055","T1112","T1497","T1059.001","T1547.001","T1027","T1564.003","T1204.001"],"references":["https:\/\/x.com\/Kb4Threatlabs\/status\/2069057429514731609"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a3999371eb0f2f2e3fb7f08","name":"Detecting the Klue supply chain attack in Salesforce instances","description":"On June 11, 2026, the Icarus threat group compromised Klue's backend systems, a market intelligence platform used by hundreds of enterprises to sync competitive battlecard data with CRM environments. The attackers exploited a dormant credential from an abandoned prototype integration to harvest OAuth tokens for Salesforce and Gong. Through automated API calls using Python scripts, the group exfiltrated CRM data including business contacts, price quotes, and sales communications from multiple customer Salesforce organizations. Klue detected the anomalous activity on June 12 and revoked OAuth credentials on June 13. The attackers subsequently launched an extortion campaign starting June 16, demanding victims contact them via Session Messenger within 48 hours.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-06-23T09:09:15.535000","created":"2026-06-22T20:21:11.668000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"Icarus","indicators":[{"id":4417670541,"indicator":"138.226.246.94","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-06-22T20:21:12","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-07-22T20:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4417670542,"indicator":"212.86.125.24","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-06-22T20:21:12","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-07-22T20:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4417670543,"indicator":"94.154.32.160","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-06-22T20:21:12","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-07-22T20:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["klue compromise","extortion campaign","crm data theft","salesforce","supply chain attack","oauth abuse"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1213.002","T1567","T1020","T1528","T1087.004","T1041","T1199","T1114.002","T1030","T1213","T1071.001","T1550.001","T1078.004"],"references":["https:\/\/securitylabs.datadoghq.com\/articles\/detecting-the-klue-supply-chain-attack-in-salesforce\/"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a3915eddc5c22f4421f124e","name":"An unknown actor distributes malicious VBS scripts via WhatsApp","description":"An active malware campaign has been discovered distributing malicious VBScript files through WhatsApp direct messages since June 2026. The operation affects users across multiple countries, with Malaysia experiencing the highest concentration of victims. Attackers compromise WhatsApp accounts and send weaponized VBS files disguised as business and financial documents to contacts. The multi-stage infection chain ultimately deploys legitimate ManageEngine Endpoint Central RMM software, providing persistent remote access to compromised systems. The scripts employ heavy obfuscation, Chinese-language comments, and modify Windows UAC settings. Infrastructure overlaps with ValleyRAT and Gh0st RAT operations suggest possible Chinese-speaking operators, though attribution remains uncertain. The campaign primarily targets individual users through opportunistic rather than focused methods, exploiting social engineering techniques with localized filenames in multiple languages.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-06-22T20:00:07.258000","created":"2026-06-22T11:01:01.331000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4182757330,"indicator":"202.61.160.201","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-06-22T11:01:02","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-07-22T11:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4370255556,"indicator":"02bb20455cc592a69c080abac770ce90","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-06-22T11:01:02","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4370255557,"indicator":"31037a42ca048e06e69a78f55bc2eff5","type":"FileHash-MD5"